# async function* made(p) { const sent = yield p }   for await (const each of made()) ..
# A yield that awaits its value by itself resumes with what was sent in, or with what the value rejects with: that arrives as a value to be thrown.
# A step of an async generator hands back a result object, a yielded value or the value the generator ended with.
# Both hand a mode back beside the value. What is taken for proven of the value without a test stands behind the mode: in an arm of the switch, or of a comparison, that is not the arm of the mode that throws,
# or where every way from the operation leads through such an arm. A cast that says nothing new, and a test, stand anywhere.
# Value and mode may go on as arguments of edges. A parameter stands for the mode where every edge that comes from the operation hands the mode on.
# FORM: Prepared
# RUN: verify
# DIAGNOSTIC: ProofInFrontOfMode 11

